Add the Kitty keyboard protocol

Implement https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/keyboard-protocol/ with its flags
1 (disambiguate), 2 (report repeat and release events) and 4 (report
alternate keys): the query CSI ? u, which replies CSI ? flags u; the push
CSI > flags u; the pop CSI < n u; and the set CSI = flags ; mode u. The main
and the alternate screen have a stack of eight entries each, and a reset
empties both. A set or a push drops the flags the library does not support,
so that a query tells the application what took effect.

Add tsm_vte_handle_key(), which takes the key's event, press, repeat or
release, and for the protocol's alternate keys the character the key gives
unshifted and the one it gives in the base layout. Without flags it sends a
press or a repeat as tsm_vte_handle_keyboard() does and a release not at
all; tsm_vte_handle_keyboard() is now a press through it. Add
tsm_vte_get_key_flags(), which returns the flags in effect.

The encoder is ported from foot's kitty_kbd_protocol() (MIT), whose notice
it carries, with kitty's choice of the keys sent as text, those with no
modifier but Shift and the locks, and of the event field, which a press
leaves out.

